      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "EARL OF PEMBROKE NZ (1) has had a series of wider or second row draws of late and did manage to come from deep on the track to win at this circuit and distance last month. This should suit and he is likely to get the favours from the inside draw. Big chance. TWISTING BY NZ (6) showed improvement here last start, coming from this barrier and racing parked before sticking on for third, beaten 4.5 metres. Owns a good third-up record so could be ready to peak. KEAYANG VIPER (8) has had to work when caught wide at her last couple but won three in a row prior so could bounce back. CLYMENUS NZ (5) should find this easier than his last two outings and has claims off a second from a similar draw here last month.",
